<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified" attributeFormDefault="unqualified" version="2.0">
  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
RESPONSE schema for getPersonCompleteDetailsB (Customer360) -- rebuilt 2026-10-12 against the
loyalty-app service generation.

Two response shapes share this document:
  1. Success -- RESPONSE_DATE + one CUSTOMER block per matched customer. NO RESPONSE_CODE is sent
     on success: the presence of CUSTOMER is the success signal.
  2. Error   -- RESPONSE_DATE + RESPONSE_CODE, no CUSTOMER. This operation sends no message or
     detail element with the code.

Transport notes
  - Every handled outcome is HTTP 200; the outcome is only in the document.
  - Service-level responses and the E899 token failure carry the ResponseId attribute.
  - E999 is a fixed fallback document: no ResponseId and an EMPTY RESPONSE_DATE.
  - The WEBSERVICE wrapper is declared because gate-level failures have been seen wrapped that
    way on sibling operations. This operation's own handler in the loyalty-app service
    generation always answers with a bare RESPONSE root.

RESPONSE_CODE catalog (xs:string ON PURPOSE -- an open set, new codes must not break validation)
  E101 XmlInput empty            E102 malformed XML
  E103 parser configuration      E104 I/O error reading the input
  E105 no usable search filter, OR no (enabled) customer matched -- the routine "not found"
       answer before enrolling a new customer
  E127 STORE_ID unknown (or no store configured when STORE_ID is omitted)
  E899 accessTokenKey validation failed (the search did not run)
  E999 unhandled failure (fixed fallback document)

All content elements are optional. Element order inside CUSTOMER and CONTACT is stable on the
loyalty-app service generation (the order used below) but is modelled as a free choice so that
differences between service generations do not break validation. An element whose value is
unknown is normally sent EMPTY rather than omitted.
    </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>

  <xs:element name="WEBSERVICE">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Wrapper seen on gate-level failures of sibling operations (WEBSERVICE/RESPONSE,
without ResponseId). Not produced by this operation's handler on the loyalty-app service generation; declared so
that such a document still validates.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType><xs:sequence>
      <xs:element ref="RESPONSE"/>
    </xs:sequence></xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="RESPONSE">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Top-level response container.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element ref="RESPONSE_DATE"/>
        <xs:element ref="CUSTOMER" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
        <xs:element ref="RESPONSE_CODE" minOccurs="0"/>
      </xs:sequence>
      <xs:attribute name="ResponseId" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Server-side request-log correlation id. Present on every response built by the
service (including E899); absent on the E999 fallback document.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:attribute>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="RESPONSE_DATE" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Server timestamp, format "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S" with 1 to 3 fractional digits
(e.g. 2026-10-12 15:01:02.655). Deliberately xs:string: not ISO 8601, and EMPTY on the E999 fallback document.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Outcome code; ABSENT on success. See the catalog in the schema header.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="CUSTOMER">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>One matched customer. Repeats when the search matched several customers
(see RECORDS_LIMIT in the request schema). Emission order: FIRST_NAME, LAST_NAME, GENDER, BIRTHDAY, CUSTOMER_ID,
REQ_REWARD_POINTS, EV_BALANCE, CASHIER, ASSIGNED_STORE, LOYALTY_STORE (conditional), PREFERRED_STORE, MKT_SEGMENTS,
CUSTOMER_CROSS_REFERENCES, POSTAL_CONTACTS, EMAIL_CONTACTS, PHONE_CONTACTS, POS_SEGMENT.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:element ref="FIRST_NAME"/>
        <xs:element ref="LAST_NAME"/>
        <xs:element ref="GENDER"/>
        <xs:element ref="BIRTHDAY"/>
        <xs:element ref="CUSTOMER_ID"/>
        <xs:element ref="REQ_REWARD_POINTS"/>
        <xs:element ref="EV_BALANCE"/>
        <xs:element ref="CASHIER"/>
        <xs:element ref="ASSIGNED_STORE"/>
        <xs:element ref="LOYALTY_STORE"/>
        <xs:element ref="PREFERRED_STORE"/>
        <xs:element ref="MKT_SEGMENTS"/>
        <xs:element ref="CUSTOMER_CROSS_REFERENCES"/>
        <xs:element ref="POSTAL_CONTACTS"/>
        <xs:element ref="EMAIL_CONTACTS"/>
        <xs:element ref="PHONE_CONTACTS"/>
        <xs:element ref="POS_SEGMENT"/>
      </xs:choice>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="FIRST_NAME" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>First name; empty when not on file.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="LAST_NAME" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Last name; empty when not on file.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="GENDER" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Value domain: MALE, FEMALE, UNKNOWN, or EMPTY when no gender is stored.
(UNKNOWN is sent when a gender is stored that is neither male nor female.) Kept as xs:string because the empty
form is routine.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="BIRTHDAY" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Stored birth date as "yyyy-MM-dd", or empty. Birthdays captured without a year
come back with a placeholder year (e.g. 0999-05-17); a birthday captured as year+month comes back on day 01.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="CUSTOMER_ID" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Customer identifier. Always populated.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="REQ_REWARD_POINTS" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Whole number: loyalty points still required to reach the reward threshold configured for the
environment (default threshold 75). "0" when the threshold is already reached or the customer has no loyalty identifier.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="EV_BALANCE" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Loyalty points balance (earned minus redeemed) as a decimal string; "0" when the
customer has no loyalty identifier. Not fixed-scale: whole numbers come back without decimals (e.g. 125), and
fractional balances may carry a long binary-fraction expansion. Parse as a decimal and round.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="CASHIER" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Cashier / operator reference stored on the customer; empty when none.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="ASSIGNED_STORE" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Store the customer is assigned to; empty when none.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="LOYALTY_STORE" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Store of loyalty enrollment. CONDITIONAL: only present when the loyalty program is
switched on for the environment AND this customer is loyalty-enabled; may then be empty.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="PREFERRED_STORE" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Customer's preferred local store; empty when none.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="POS_SEGMENT" type="xs:string">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Point-of-sale segment code for the customer; empty when none.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="MKT_SEGMENTS">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Marketing segments of the customer, newest first. Present but EMPTY when the customer
has none. The number of entries is capped by an environment setting (default 2).</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType><xs:sequence>
      <xs:element name="MKT_SEGMENT" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Segment identifier.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:sequence></xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="CUSTOMER_CROSS_REFERENCES">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>External identifiers of the customer. Present but EMPTY when there are none to show.
Only a fixed set of identifier types is returned (others on file are not exposed), and LOYALTY_ID is withheld
unless the customer is loyalty-enabled.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType><xs:sequence>
      <xs:element name="CROSS_REFERENCE" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:complexType>
          <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
            <xs:element name="SYSTEM_REFERENCE" type="xs:string">
              <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Identifier type. Returned types include LOYALTY_ID, POS_ID, APTOS_ID, DW_ID,
ATG_CUST_ID, CHEETAHMAIL_ID, LEGACY_ID, WINDSS_ID, AFFINITY_ID, HARTEHANKS_ID, HH_HOUSEHOLD_ID, plus the type named in
the request's SYSTEM_REFERENCE where that is a brand-specific type. Open value set.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
            </xs:element>
            <xs:element name="SYSTEM_REFERENCE_ID" type="xs:string">
              <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Identifier value.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
            </xs:element>
          </xs:choice>
        </xs:complexType>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:sequence></xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="POSTAL_CONTACTS">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>The customer's current primary/general postal address. ALWAYS carries exactly one
CONTACT: when no address is on file it is a placeholder with empty fields and BAD_POSTAL_ADDRESS_STATUS = Y.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType><xs:sequence>
      <xs:element ref="CONTACT" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
    </xs:sequence></xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="EMAIL_CONTACTS">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>The customer's current primary e-mail address. ALWAYS carries exactly one CONTACT:
when no primary e-mail is on file -- or it is withheld by the environment's solicitation settings -- it is a
placeholder with empty EMAIL, BAD_EMAIL_ADDRESS_STATUS = Y and ALLOW_SOLICITATION = Y. An empty EMAIL therefore
means "nothing to show"; do not read the placeholder's flags as consent.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType><xs:sequence>
      <xs:element ref="CONTACT" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
    </xs:sequence></xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:element name="PHONE_CONTACTS">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>The customer's current primary phone. Unlike the other two groups there is NO
placeholder: the container is EMPTY when no primary phone is on file or it is withheld by solicitation settings.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType><xs:sequence>
      <xs:element ref="CONTACT" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
    </xs:sequence></xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:element name="CONTACT">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>One contact entry. Which children appear depends on the parent group:
  POSTAL_CONTACTS: TO_NAME, ADDRESS1, ADDRESS2, CITY, STATE, ZIPCODE, COUNTRY, CONTACT_MECH_ID,
                   BAD_POSTAL_ADDRESS_STATUS, ALLOW_SOLICITATION, CONTACT_TYPE
  EMAIL_CONTACTS:  EMAIL, CONTACT_MECH_ID, BAD_EMAIL_ADDRESS_STATUS, ALLOW_SOLICITATION, CONTACT_TYPE
  PHONE_CONTACTS:  PHONE, CONTACT_MECH_ID, ALLOW_SOLICITATION, CONTACT_TYPE</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:element name="TO_NAME" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Addressee name; empty when not stored.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="ADDRESS1" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Address line 1; empty when not stored.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="ADDRESS2" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Address line 2; empty when not stored.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="CITY" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>City; empty when not stored.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="STATE" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>State / province code; empty when not stored.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="ZIPCODE" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Postal code, upper-cased; empty when not stored. The postal-code extension is not returned.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="COUNTRY" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Country code as stored (e.g. CAN); empty when not stored.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="EMAIL" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>E-mail address; empty on the placeholder entry.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="PHONE" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Phone number: stored area code immediately followed by the number, no separators and no country code.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="CONTACT_MECH_ID" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Identifier of this contact record; send it back in updateCustomerB to update or expire
this exact record. Empty on a placeholder entry.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="BAD_POSTAL_ADDRESS_STATUS" type="YesNo">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Y = address NOT confirmed deliverable; N = address verified. N requires both a
positive address-verification record for the customer and the address not being flagged undeliverable. Y on the placeholder entry.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="BAD_EMAIL_ADDRESS_STATUS" type="YesNo">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Y = e-mail flagged undeliverable (or placeholder entry); N = not flagged.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="ALLOW_SOLICITATION" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Marketing consent for this contact. Value domain: Y (allowed), N (not allowed),
U (unknown / never asked), or EMPTY (nothing stored; always empty on the postal placeholder entry). Brand-level
consent for the request's store takes precedence over the contact-level value where one exists. Kept as
xs:string: the value is passed through from stored data and is not limited to Y/N.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="CONTACT_TYPE" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Fixed per group: PRIMARY_LOCATION (postal -- also used when the stored purpose is the
general location), PRIMARY_EMAIL, PRIMARY_PHONE. Empty on a placeholder entry.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:choice>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>

  <xs:simpleType name="YesNo">
    <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Y or N. These two status flags are always sent with one of the two values.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="Y"/>
      <xs:enumeration value="N"/>
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>
</xs:schema>
